SUMMARY:River Critters and Pond Pals (Matthews)
DESCRIPTION:Have you ever seen a dragonfly in the winter? How about a mayfly? Where do these animals go once it turns cold\, and where do they come from when it starts to warm up? Examining freshwater macroinvertebrates can reveal many important features about their habitat. They are storytellers about the health of an ecoystem. Are there pollutants in the water? Let’s ask the leeches. Do these waters support lots of species? Let’s ask the caddisfly. \nJoin HAWK and Great Outdoors University for a stream based educational event including a special hands-on stream exploration for kids and families! There will be many specimens to observe\, a scientific key to identify species\, and a game to match the larval form to the adult form. Registration is required for this morning of adventurous fun at Squirrel Lake Park. \nPRE-REGISTRATION FOR THE STREAM EXPLORATION IS REQUIRED. \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://ncwf.org/event/river-critters-and-pond-pals-matthews/
CATEGORIES:Featured
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncwf.org/wp-content/uploads/RiverCrittersPondPals26.jpg
END:VEVENT
